🟦 1. What is Amazon CloudWatch? (Deep Dive)

Amazon CloudWatch is a centralized monitoring service in AWS used for:

✔ Monitoring EC2 performance (CPU, RAM, Disk IO, Network)
✔ Monitoring RDS, DynamoDB, Lambda, API Gateway
✔ Collecting Application Logs from EC2, ECS, EKS
✔ Creating Dashboards
✔ Triggering alarms for automation
✔ Creating custom metrics
✔ Cost + Billing alarms
✔ Real-time log queries using Log Insights

