🟦 3. CloudWatch Namespace + Metrics + Dashboard
✔ What is a Namespace?

A Namespace is a container that stores related metrics.

Examples:

Service	Namespace
EC2	AWS/EC2
RDS	AWS/RDS
Load Balancer	AWS/ApplicationELB
Lambda	AWS/Lambda
Custom Metrics	Custom/<your-app>

If you create custom metrics using CLI, they must be stored inside:

--namespace "Custom/EC2App"

✔ What is a Metric?

A metric is a time-ordered set of data points.

Examples:

CPUUtilization

NetworkIn

NetworkOut

DiskReadOps

RequestCount

Latency

For EC2 → metrics are collected every 5 min (standard) or 1 min (detailed monitoring).

✔ CloudWatch Dashboard

A dashboard is a customized monitoring screen.

You can add:

Graphs

Line charts

Single-number widgets

Custom metrics

Logs widgets

How to create Dashboard (Steps)

Open → CloudWatch

Go to Dashboards

Click → “Create Dashboard”

Add widgets:
✔ Line
✔ Stacked area
✔ Number
✔ Text

Choose metrics (e.g., CPUUtilization)

Save dashboard

Example: Dashboard for EC2 Monitoring

Widgets include:

✔ CPU Utilization Graph
✔ Memory Utilization (via agent)
✔ Disk Usage (via agent)
✔ Network Bandwidth

Memory / Disk metrics require CloudWatch agent.

🟥 4. CloudWatch Alarm (Trigger Alerts)

(VERY IMPORTANT for interview)

An alarm monitors a metric and sends notification if threshold is crossed.

✔ Types of Alarms
1. Static Alarm

CPU > 80%

2. Anomaly Detection Alarm

CloudWatch learns pattern and alerts outside normal range.

3. Composite Alarm

Combination of 2 or more alarms.
Used for production environments to prevent false alerts.

✔ CloudWatch Alarm Workflow (Diagram)
Metric → Alarm → SNS Topic → Email/SMS/Slack/Lambda

✔ Example: Create CPU > 80% Alarm

Threshold:

CPUUtilization

GreaterThanThreshold

80%

2 datapoints out of 3

Actions:

Send Email (SNS)

Stop Instance (optional)

Auto scale (optional)

🟧 5. Billing Alarm (Mandatory for every AWS Account)

Billing alarms work on EstimatedCharges metric inside the special namespace:

AWS/Billing


⚠ Billing metric is only available in US East (N. Virginia) Region

Steps to Create Billing Alarm

Go → CloudWatch

Region set to us-east-1

Metrics → Billing

Choose: EstimatedCharges

Set threshold → e.g., > ₹500

Send SNS email

🟫 6. Composite Alarms (Deep Explanation)

Composite alarm = combines multiple alarms using Boolean logic (AND/OR)

Example:

CPUAlarm

NetworkAlarm

Composite Alarm triggers only when:

CPUAlarm == ALARM AND NetworkAlarm == ALARM


Use-case:

✔ Reduce false positives
✔ Trigger only when system failure is confirmed
✔ High reliability systems

🟦 7. CloudWatch Agent (Install & Configure)

Default EC2 metrics DO NOT include:

❌ RAM Usage
❌ Disk Usage
❌ Disk Space %
❌ Processes
❌ Application Logs

For this CloudWatch Agent is required.

Install Agent (Amazon Linux)
sudo yum install amazon-cloudwatch-agent -y

Create config file
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-config-wizard


You select:

✔ CPU
✔ Memory
✔ Disk
✔ Logs

Output is stored at:

/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.json

Start Agent
sudo systemctl start amazon-cloudwatch-agent
sudo systemctl enable amazon-cloudwatch-agent


Now → Memory & Disk metrics appear in:

CWAgent Namespace

🟩 8. Sending Application Logs to CloudWatch (Full Deep Dive)

You want logs → CloudWatch → Log Group → Log Streams.

Example path:

/var/log/nginx/access.log
/var/log/app/app.log


Add in agent config:

"logs": {
  "logs_collected": {
    "files": {
      "collect_list": [
        {
          "file_path": "/var/log/app.log",
          "log_group_name": "AppLogs",
          "log_stream_name": "{instance_id}"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}


Restart Agent:

sudo systemctl restart amazon-cloudwatch-agent

🟧 9. CloudWatch Log Insights (Execute Queries on Logs)

CloudWatch Log Insights is like SQL for logs.

🔥 Important Queries Example
1. Find error events
fields @timestamp, @message
| filter @message like /ERROR/
| sort @timestamp desc

2. Count errors per hour
stats count(*) by bin(1h)

3. Find IPs making most requests
fields @message
| parse @message "[ip=*] *" as client_ip
| stats count(*) by client_ip

4. Latency analysis
filter latency > 200
| stats avg(latency) by url

🟥 10. Create Alarm Based on Logs (IMPORTANT)

Log metric filter → creates Custom Metric → Alarm can be configured.

Example: Trigger alarm when the word “ERROR” appears

CloudWatch Logs → Log Group

Create Metric Filter

Filter pattern:

ERROR


Assign to namespace:

Custom/ErrorLogs


Metric name: ErrorCount

Create Alarm → if ErrorCount > 0

🟩 11. Creating Custom Metrics (Using CLI)

Custom metric → your own application sends data to CloudWatch.

CLI Example: Send random CPU metric
aws cloudwatch put-metric-data \
  --metric-name AppCPU \
  --namespace Custom/MyApp \
  --value 42

With Dimensions
aws cloudwatch put-metric-data \
  --metric-name RequestCount \
  --namespace Custom/WebApp \
  --dimensions InstanceID=i-123456 \
  --value 10

🟦 12. CloudWatch Cleanup (Remove unused resources)
Delete Log Groups
aws logs delete-log-group --log-group-name "/aws/ec2/app"

Delete Alarms
aws cloudwatch delete-alarms --alarm-names CPUAlarm

Delete Dashboard
aws cloudwatch delete-dashboards --dashboard-names MyDashboard

Delete Metric Filters
aws logs delete-metric-filter \
  --log-group-name AppLogs \
  --filter-name ErrorFilter

